{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/922123-bloodline-childer-of-the-morrigan-2e","id":922123,"title":"Bloodline: Childer of the Morrigan [2E]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-27T11:44:41-07:00","id":922123,"title":"Bloodline: Childer of the Morrigan [2E]","content":"Hello, fellow fans! Recently I wrote two submissions for OP and sent one of them. This is the other, and since it is just laying around, I figured I might as well show it here! It was done with the 1000 words limit, so it might be too brief at parts, but I have a lot of ideas for the Childer based on this write-up!<br /> <br /> I hope you enjoy it! <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:32px\">Childer of the Morrigan</span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><i>The disabling paranoia in a packed nightclub and sliver of a crescent in the night sky. A beloved mortal suddenly taken by illness, daysleeps filled with broken corpses and hungry ravens. The chilling sound of silence in the woods, the regret of selling out for fear of the Lance. Rake marks along the porch, the stirring of one\u2019s Beast as it is preyed upon. The dread of not being alone in one\u2019s haven.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">For as long as vampires have sacrificed the living in distant groves there have been dark wings soaring overhead, silently guarding those who worship the Crone. Often reminding vampires of the Birds of Dis, the fear such association elicits in Kindred hearts suits these monsters well, for when a murder of Stormcrows takes flight it is never a warning: a Requiem will end that night.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">As the All Night Society understands it the Circle of the Crone is a newly-blooded covenant born of unwholesome worship and Sanctified bonfires but the Morrigans have been part of the Long Night for as long as any elder can remember. Birthed cawing in the lost bogs of northern Ireland the Childer are known to arrive unannounced to swear Requiem-long oaths to those infected by the insidious sorcery of Cr\u00faac. Some say the blood spilled to the old gods is what gives the Stormcrows their power, while others whisper that tainted vitae is the only blood a Morrigan Beast will ever settle for.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Strong where the Masquerade is weak, the Childer hunt the enemies of the Circle like their continued existence is an affront to the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><i>morr\u00edgna</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">, the blackness of a frenzied Morrigan\u2019s eyes betraying nothing but fury. When a Childer is on the hunt she can take nights, or even weeks, before ending the agonizing danse with unwilling prey. That everything around the dead man walking seems to crumble is an eerie similarity to the omens that follow owl sightings, a coincidence many Kindred do not miss.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">The Becoming:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Anyone can be chosen by the Morrigan if they have suffered enough. Martial prowess can be taught but true fortitude is earned in agony. For this reason Stormcrows are seldom Embraced young, and while it is true the bloodline is almost entirely female that is more due to reverence to the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><i>morr\u00edgna's</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"> favored forms than anything else. The Embrace is harrowing, heralded by omens and tragedies until it culminates in the death of a prospect, and quickly a newly-minted monster is left to fend off for herself as it learns about her limits. The Morrigans believe blood and guile will teach a young Childe and patiently wait until blood sympathy leads their spawn back to them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">In the Danse Macabre: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">The Childer of the Morrigan lead lonely Requiems. Their rituals are personal and their worship is vexing even to covenant sisters. Their loyal nature makes them too strong an ally to the Circle for outsiders to be comfortable with, and this tension between covenants, in turn, feeds the the worshippers of the Crone and draws them closer together.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">The only stance a prince will gladly welcome Morrigans in is when beset by Strix. Unlike most Kindred the Childer seem more than eager to die fighting an owl and the more powerful the foe, more Stormcrows seem to flock to take it down, no matter the cost. Many domains turned into cloisters that way.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Bloodline Bane: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Cr\u00faac is alive and it lures these vampires by singing the dark lullaby of their shared womb. Each point of blood used in a ritual that the Morrigan then consumes allows her to use willpower for a week. Otherwise a Stormcrow simply doesn\u2019t feel the fire within to give it her all, and may not spend willpower points.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Nickname: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Stormcrows, Morrigans</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Clan: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Gangrel</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Bloodline Disciplines: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Animalism, Protean, Resilience and Vigor</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Bloodline Gift: Dark Mother\u2019s Caress</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">The vampire can spend a willpower and one point of vitae to anoint herself or another with blood used in Cr\u00faac. Once marked she gains a bonus to her Resistance rolls equal to the Morrigan's Blood Potency for the night.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Badhb</b> Catha\u2019s Talon (Protean \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">This Devotion turns a Stormcrow\u2019s Horrid Claws into blackened, gnarly instruments of sacrifice. Whenever she strikes a vampire her foe bleeds one vitae, and then another point the next turn. The spilled blood may be used for Cr\u00faac if a sorcerer is performing in the vicinities. For as long as she bleeds the victim suffers from the Distracted condition as the underworld calls to her.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Raise the Soulbeast (Animalism \u2022\u2022, Protean \u2022)</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">The Morrigan spends four vitae and births the crow of her own flesh. The creature receives the benefits of Undead Familiar and may merge with the Stormcrow like the vampire is an Unmarked Grave. It must rest within the vampire every day or die, but otherwise exists without demanding more vitae like a familiar would. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Additionally, It is considered to be twice removed from any Cr\u00faac practitioner for any blood sympathy rolls to detect and find witches in a domain. This is not real blood sympathy, but a mystic link between of the Stormcrows and the vile sorcery itself.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Her Sister's Keeper (Resilience \u2022\u2022)</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">In times of great duress a Stormcrow cannot be everywhere. The vampire spends one vitae when someone marked with by her bloodline gift is attacked to make herself the target instead, even if the Morrigan isn\u2019t physically close to the confrontation. She may activate Resilience as normal to mitigate the blow, but the phantasmal damage ignores any mundane armor.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Cloak of Nemain (Vigor \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">The Morrigan Requiem is an eternal crucible, and in agony there is enlightenment. This wisdom feeds her tortured body by allowing a Stormcrow to reap the suffering she wreaks. The vampire spends two vitae and falls into frenzy (although she may attempt to ride it). For the remainder of the scene any blood shed by her claws may be used to heal the vampire, reflexively, as if vitae was spent from her own reserves. This does not count against her limits per turn.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":11263,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","user":"Gimmisky","date":". 09-18-2016, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}